From e4eb302b6fa30f3211e4c0dbe50fcb81d6b581e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: davmels <davmelous@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 07:59:52 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 59/61] ScienceWorld environment: native multi-turn episodes in
 the Apertus 2 format

ScienceWorld (AllenAI, Apache-2.0) simulates 30 elementary-school science tasks as a text game on the
JVM. The scienceworld environment plays one episode per rollout sample: the row prompt holds the task
and the first observation, every burst gives one command (reply frame or act tool call, per row), and
the simulator answer comes back as a user message or a call result. Invalid commands return the
simulator text and the episode goes on. Reward per turn is the change of max(score, 0)/100, so an
episode totals its last score in [0, 1].

Simulators run in worker actors with one JVM each, placed on the nodes of the placement groups that
env.scienceworld.placement_group_prefix names (the vLLM nodes). A worker runs one simulator call at a
time: two loads at once in one JVM fail on the global simplification state. Episode metadata carries
the commands so far, so a lost episode is replayed.

Rollouts take an observation token_ids from the environment when it gives them (input frames encoded
by apertus-common); otherwise they tokenize the text as before. Frame metrics are averaged per name
over the samples that report them, in rollouts and in validation, since ScienceWorld reports other
counts than the math environment. New processor apertus2_sciworld_data_processor.

